Source: amber-agent
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jacek Trefon <hello@trefon.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               libcurl4-openssl-dev,
               libncurses-dev,
               pkgconf
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/jtrefon/amber
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/jtrefon/amber.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/jtrefon/amber

Package: amber-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# The pre-repository packages were built with fpm and installed the same
# binaries from a package called `amber`. A version-scoped conflict replaces
# those and leaves Debian's unrelated `amber` (a different program, /usr/bin/amberc
# only) installable.
Conflicts: amber (>= 0.1.0)
Replaces: amber (>= 0.1.0)
Description: AI agent harness with a terminal interface and a headless CLI
 amber runs an agent loop against any OpenAI-compatible endpoint: the model
 reads and writes files, searches the project and runs approval-gated commands
 while the session, context and tool output are rendered in place.
 .
 This package carries the runtime: the full-screen client (amber), the headless
 client (amber-cli), the bundled plugins and the data tree they read at startup.

Package: amber-agent-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: amber-agent (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: development files for the amber agent harness
 Headers, static libraries and the pkg-config file needed to build a tool, a
 plugin or an embedding application against the amber core.
 .
 Build with: pkg-config --cflags --libs amber-agent

Package: amber-agent-bench
Section: devel
Architecture: any
Depends: amber-agent (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: benchmark and KPI harness for the amber agent
 amber-bench runs scenario suites against the harness and scores the result.
 Hermetic runs use a deterministic fake model, so they are safe in CI; live runs
 target any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
 .
 The package ships the scenario corpus and the model profiles, which the harness
 resolves from the install prefix rather than the working directory.

Package: amber-agent-release
Section: admin
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: signed package repository configuration for amber-agent
 Installs the archive signing key at
 /usr/share/keyrings/amber-agent-archive-keyring.gpg and the deb822 source
 definition with a Signed-By that points at it.
 .
 Installing this package and running "apt-get update" is equivalent to what the
 published install script does, without fetching a script first.
